@startuml Topic1_Agents_vs_Workflows_vs_Chatbots
title Topic 1 - Agents vs Workflows vs Chatbots\n(Defining question: WHO controls the control flow, and WHEN?)

skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam roundcorner 12

start

:Incoming task / request;

if (Can the full sequence of steps\nbe written in advance?) then (YES - path is knowable)
  if (Does it need any tools / actions,\nor just a text reply?) then (Just text in -> out)
    #LightBlue:**CHATBOT**;
    note right
      * Stateless text generator
      * NO tools, NO memory beyond context
      * Cannot act in the world
    end note
  else (Needs fixed sequence of steps)
    #LightGreen:**DETERMINISTIC WORKFLOW**;
    note right
      * Developer fixes control flow at DESIGN TIME
      * Model only fills in content
      * Model NEVER decides what happens next
      * "compile time": path fixed in advance
      * TRAP: Prompt chaining LOOKS agentic
        but is STILL a workflow
    end note
  endif
else (NO - path must adapt)
  #Orange:**AGENTIC SYSTEM**;
  note right
    * Control flow EMERGES at RUNTIME
    * Model chooses next step from its reasoning
    * DEFINING TRAIT: runtime tool selection
    * Higher autonomy = higher cost + risk
  end note
endif

:== ACTION-ENVIRONMENT GAP ==\n* Native output = TEXT only\n* Can DESCRIBE an action, cannot DO it\n* BRIDGE across the gap = TOOL USE;

:== AUGMENTED LLM ==\n1. Retrieval -> what it KNOWS\n2. Tools -> what it can DO\n3. Memory -> what it REMEMBERS\n* Single agent = augmented LLM in a loop\n* Build agents LESS often than you think;

stop

@enduml